 "drivingQuestion": "From where must one read the Megilla to fulfil the obligation?",
 "outcome": "not_dialectical",
 "outcomeNote": "Mishna with a three-way dispute",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "megillah.19a.4",
   "daf": "19a",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ בֶּן עִיר שֶׁהָלַךְ לִכְרַךְ וּבֶן כְּרַךְ שֶׁהָלַךְ לְעִיר, אִם עָתִיד לַחְזוֹר לִמְקוֹמוֹ — קוֹרֵא כִּמְקוֹמוֹ, וְאִם לָאו — קוֹרֵא עִמָּהֶן.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» With regard to «a resident of an» unwalled «town who went to a walled city,» where the Megilla is read on the fifteenth of Adar, and conversely, «a resident of a walled city who went to an» unwalled «town» where it is read on the fourteenth, the following distinction applies: «If he is destined to return to his» original «place, he reads» it «according to» the halakha governing «his» own «place, and if not,» i.e., if he is not destined to return to his place, «he reads with them,» the residents of his current location."
  },
  {
   "id": "megillah.19a.5",
   "daf": "19a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "וּמֵהֵיכָן קוֹרֵא אָדָם אֶת הַמְּגִילָּה וְיוֹצֵא בָּהּ יְדֵי חוֹבָה? רַבִּי מֵאִיר אוֹמֵר: כּוּלָּהּ. רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: מֵ״אִישׁ יְהוּדִי״. רַבִּי יוֹסֵי אוֹמֵר: מֵ״אַחַר הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה״.",
   "en": "Beginning «from where must a person read the Megilla in order to fulfill his obligation? Rabbi Meir says:» He must read «all of it. Rabbi Yehuda says:» He need read only «from» “There was «a certain Jew”» (Esther 2:5). «Rabbi Yosei says: From “After these things”» (Esther 3:1)."
  }
 ],
